<title>USA: Ford sport/utility vehicle production continues.</title>
<headline>Ford sport/utility vehicle production continues.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said production of its Expedition full-size sport/utility vehicle is continuing Tuesday despite a strike by United Auto Workers union members at a key supplier's nearby seat plant.</p>
<p>&quot;Michigan Truck is up and running,&quot; said Francine Romine-MacBride, a spokeswoman for Ford, referring to the Michigan Truck Assembly plant in Wayne, Mich.</p>
<p>About 300 newly-organized UAW workers walked off the job at Johnson Control Inc's plant in Plymouth, Mich., at 0600-EST Tuesday. The union and Milwaukee, Wis.-based company are at odds over terms of a new contract.</p>
</text>
